35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The closeout files are sobering. Catalogue-style awards still draw users a decade later, while mechanism-focused ones often end unresolved.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The staffing data is stark. Phenotyping technicians are gone, but modelling applicants are arriving. Yet, our senior analysts are seconded abroad until autumn.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks. One engineer covers three institutes. This is a critical bottleneck for any project relying on that equipment.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The ledgers confirm my suspicion: shipping costs are up, but glasshouse subsidies remain. Computing is free, yet animal day rates have spiked.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The field sites lost whole seasons to weather, but indoor rooms ran uninterrupted. This suggests we should prioritize projects that can be conducted safely indoors to avoid these delays.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"Ryuji, your staffing concerns are valid, but the closeout files suggest we should favor projects with lasting utility over those chasing fleeting mechanisms.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, lasting utility is vital, but I must address the immediate capacity gap. With senior analysts abroad, computational projects face a severe staffing bottleneck right now.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, the spectroscopy suite’s eleven-week idle period is a direct infrastructure failure, not just a staffing issue. We cannot assume computational feasibility if the hardware is unreliable.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the hardware gap is real, but the financials are clearer. Simulation is now free, while animal costs have spiked. We should weigh that against the staffing risks.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, the spectroscopy delay is worrying, but the field site losses are more frequent. We should prioritize indoor work to avoid weather-related interruptions.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, I hear your caution. Yet the portfolio review shows computation-based projects rarely stall, unlike those relying on live colonies.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, that data is reassuring. However, the minutes confirm both senior analysts are absent until autumn. We cannot rely on computation alone if the people to run it are gone.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, the staffing gap is real, but the hardware failure is worse. Eleven weeks idle means the equipment itself is the bottleneck, not just the people.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, the absence is temporary. The financial shift is structural. Free simulation versus spiked animal costs is a permanent reality we must price in.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, the analysts return in autumn. But the field sites are gone for the season. We must choose a project that can start indoors immediately.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I agree. The closeout files show catalogue-style work endures, while mechanism-focused projects often stall. We should favor lasting utility over fleeting insights.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, I agree on the indoor priority. The glasshouse crew is intact, unlike the missing technicians. We must fund work that can actually start now.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Midori, I must object. The glasshouse blocks are booked solid for two cycles. Indoor work is impossible there. We must avoid greenhouse-dependent projects entirely.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, that contradicts the subsidy data. Glasshouse bench fees are still covered centrally. The booking pressure is real, but the cost isn't.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, I hear your concern about the bookings. However, the field site losses were due to weather, not capacity. We need a project that avoids both external weather risks and saturated shared equipment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
